      "writtenOn": "2026-09-08T23:54:06Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "The `size_t` all over the place seems a little convoluted. Could we do something like:\n```\nDoWorkChunked(\n  pool,\n  const std::vector\u003cTarget*\u003e\u0026 targets,\n  size_t chunk_size,\n  const std::function\u003cvoid(std::vector\u003cTarget*\u003e::iterator, std::vector\u003cTarget*\u003e::iterator)\u003e\u0026 work);\n```\n\nIt\u0027s a little more verbose, but I think it\u0027s far more clear how it works just from looking at the signature.",
      "revId": "9468668ff05a5f74a28f6c050474f48828f34f60",
      "serverId": "c360c8e5-7aa8-3905-a7a0-810934766dac"
    },
    {
